    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0387" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3739: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-01-28T07:08:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-01-27T11:00:00+04:53"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 28, 1919, 7:08
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>“58, January 27, 11 a.m. Referring my January 25th, 5 p.m.<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d300-f1"/> It appears now definitely arranged that Czech troops are
                    to be withdrawn and placed at strategic points from Ekaterinburg and Cheliabinsk
                        <pb facs="0388" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/> to Irkutsk to guard railroad and
                    prevent Bolsheviks uprising. The plan is excellent providing Czech soldiers
                    agree to it. Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
